From 4cd93a3ea2dedc24f8b047bb08db28faeced4fce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <PanditRitesh@JohnDeere.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:22:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 001/140] feat: downloads for links and Jellyfin, light-mode
 chip fix, M3 search

Downloads:
- Queue-based downloader built on Ketch with per-download progress
  notifications (pause/resume/cancel) and a yt-dlp foreground-service
  engine for HLS/DASH/extractor links
- Downloads screen with queue controls and SAF download-location picker,
  reachable from the Network and Jellyfin top bars
- Jellyfin: per-episode, season and whole-series downloads; external
  subtitles saved as sidecar files next to the video; downloaded badges;
  offline-first playback of completed downloads with their subtitles
- Network tab: recents-row download action and Play Link sheet download
  button (direct links -> queue, m3u8/mpd/extractor -> yt-dlp, magnets ->
  torrent flow)

Fixes:
- 4K/HDR overlay chips and watch-progress fills were invisible in light
  mode (primary-on-black scrim); now use the always-dark accent scheme

UI:
- InlineSearchBar rewritten on Material 3 SearchBar/InputField with proper
  IME Search handling; migrated remaining custom search fields (settings
  search, mpv help, codec list, torrent selection)
- New strings translated for all bundled locales
